concept:australian-heritage-commission-short-title-amendment-act-1976-sec-3 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "3 Section 3"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-3 ;
    values:originalText "Section 3 of the Principal Act is amended— interpret­ ation. (a) by inserting in sub-section (1), before the definition of “Australia”, the following definition: — “ ‘Aboriginals’ means persons who are— (a) members of the Aboriginal race of Australia; or (b) members of the race to which Torres Strait Islanders belong; ”; and (b) by omitting from sub-section (1) the definition of “ representa­ tive Commissioner” and substituting the following definition:— “ ‘representative Commissioner’ means a Commissioner whose appointment is authorized by sub-section 12 (1 A );” . 4. Section 7 of the Principal Act is amended by omitting paragraph Functions of (a) and substituting the following paragraph:— Commission. “ (a) to furnish advice to the Minister, either of its own motion or upon request made to it by the Minister, on matters relating to the national estate, including advice relating to action to con­ serve, improve and present the national estate; ”.  No. 135 Australian Heritage Commission Amendment Consultation Commission." ;
    skos:definition "Section 3 of the Principal Act is amended— interpret­ ation. (a) by inserting in sub-section (1), before the definition of “Australia”, the following definition: — “ ‘Aboriginals’ means persons who are— (a) members of the Aboriginal race of Australia; or (b) members of the race to which Torres Strait Islanders belong; ”; and (b) by omitting from sub-section (1) the definition of “ representa­ tive Commissioner” and substituting the following definition:— “ ‘representative Commissioner’ means a Commissioner whose appointment is authorized by sub-section 12 (1 A );” . 4. Section 7 of the Principal Act is amended by omitting paragraph Functions of (a) and substituting the following paragraph:— Commission. “ (a) to furnish advice to the Minister, either of its own motion or upon request made to it by the Minister, on matters relating to the national estate, including advice relating to action to con­ serve, improve and present the national estate; ”.  No. 135 Australian Heritage Commission Amendment Consultation Commission."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "b5d70e547975d8a65d02e2e4b70a568665a84948e5104a47eb3429c190a598a0" ;
    cof:pageNumber "1"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Definition of Aboriginals inserted into sub-section (1) of Section 3." ;
