doc:sec-6-ss-2 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "6(2) Section 6" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(2) The person who was, immediately before the commencement of this Act, the Chairman of the Commission continues to be the Chairman of the Commission as if he had been appointed as the Chairman under the Principal Act as amended by this Act and holds office, subject to the Principal Act as amended by this Act, for the remainder of the period of his appointment under the Principal Act." ;
    cof:pageNumber "2"^^xsd:integer .

concept:australian-heritage-commission-short-title-amendment-act-1976-sec-6-ss-3 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "6(3) Section 6"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-6-ss-3 ;
    values:originalText "(3) A person who held office as a Commissioner other than the Chairman immediately before the commencement of this Act continues to hold office as a Commissioner as if he had been appointed as a Com­ missioner under the Principal Act as amended by this Act and, if he was appointed for a specified period, holds office, subject to the Principal Act as amended by this Act, for the remainder of the period of his appoint­ ment under the Principal Act.  Australian Heritage Commission Amendment No. 135 7. Section 23 of the Principal Act is amended by adding at the end Entry of thereof the following sub-section: — Register “ (5) The Commission shall not take any action under this section in relation to a place for reasons relating only to the association of the place with the history, culture or beliefs of Aboriginals unless— (a) the place is a site specially protected under a law of a State or Territory by reason of its association with the history, culture or beliefs of Aboriginals; or (b) the action is taken in accordance with a direction of the Minister under section 25 or the recommendation of a person or organization approved by the Minister for the purposes of this sub-section.”." ;
    skos:definition "(3) A person who held office as a Commissioner other than the Chairman immediately before the commencement of this Act continues to hold office as a Commissioner as if he had been appointed as a Com­ missioner under the Principal Act as amended by this Act and, if he was appointed for a specified period, holds office, subject to the Principal Act as amended by this Act, for the remainder of the period of his appoint­ ment under the Principal Act.  Australian Heritage Commission Amendment No. 135 7. Section 23 of the Principal Act is amended by adding at the end Entry of thereof the following sub-section: — Register “ (5) The Commission shall not take any action under this section in relation to a place for reasons relating only to the association of the place with the history, culture or beliefs of Aboriginals unless— (a) the place is a site specially protected under a law of a State or Territory by reason of its association with the history, culture or beliefs of Aboriginals; or (b) the action is taken in accordance with a direction of the Minister under section 25 or the recommendation of a person or organization approved by the Minister for the purposes of this sub-section.”."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "d4c0bbef9b9812a27c1dc97cfc667a495c25ed1f54757a10882af9e2fd42799c" ;
    values:partOf concept:australian-heritage-commission-short-title-amendment-act-1976-sec-6 ;
    cof:pageNumber "2"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "A person who held office as a Commissioner continues to hold office." ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
